# Copy to Replit Secrets (never commit real values).
#
# === How to access internal admin (API only in this repo) ===
#
# 1) Set INTERNAL_API_SECRET on the MAIN app to a long random string; restart the server.
# 2) Base URL = wherever the Express API is served (same host as /api/*). Examples:
#      http://127.0.0.1:5000   (local main app default PORT)
#      https://your-repl.yourname.replit.app
#    Do NOT use a placeholder string like YOUR_MAIN_APP_ORIGIN — that is not a real hostname.
# 3) Every /api/internal/* request must include header:
#      X-Internal-API-Key: <same value as INTERNAL_API_SECRET>
# 4) Full admin REST tree is under EITHER path (same handlers):
#      GET/POST/PATCH/DELETE  <base>/api/internal/admin/...
#      GET/POST/PATCH/DELETE  <base>/api/admin/...
#    Public discovery (no auth): GET <base>/api/openapi.json
#    Example (do not paste real secrets into shell history; use env var):
#      curl -sS -H "X-Internal-API-Key: $INTERNAL_API_SECRET" \
#        "$BYANAI_BASE/api/internal/health"
#      curl -sS -H "X-Internal-API-Key: $INTERNAL_API_SECRET" \
#        "$BYANAI_BASE/api/internal/admin/billing/overview"
# 5) Smoke test from repo root (artifacts/loop23):
#      cd artifacts/loop23 && npm run verify:internal-api -- https://YOUR_MAIN_API_HOST
#    With secret: INTERNAL_API_SECRET=... npm run verify:internal-api -- https://YOUR_MAIN_API_HOST
# 6) Admin CP UI (artifacts/loop23-admincp) — process must be running:
#      cd artifacts/loop23-admincp && pnpm run build
#      INTERNAL_API_SECRET=same-as-main BYANAI_API_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:5000 pnpm run start
#    Default listen: ADMIN_PORT, or PORT (Replit), or 5050. UI URL path defaults to /cp/control/
#    Example: https://your-host.replit.dev/cp/control/
#
#    Replit: the public https://....replit.dev URL usually maps to process.env.PORT only.
#    Do not add :5050 to that hostname unless Replit’s “Ports” panel exposes 5050 separately.
#    Set TRUST_PROXY=1 in Secrets for correct HTTPS/cookies. Set BYANAI_API_BASE_URL to your
#    *main* Byan AI app’s public https origin (the API that serves /api/internal), not this Repl
#    unless the main app runs here too.
#
# --- Main Byan AI app (Express + PostgreSQL; artifacts/loop23) ---
# Required for /api/internal/* and /api/internal/admin/*
INTERNAL_API_SECRET=
# Optional: public support bridge /api/public/support/* for external admin
SUPPORT_API_KEY=
# Holds all user/billing/support rows
DATABASE_URL=
#
# --- loopcp admin Replit (separate project; exact names depend on that repo) ---
# Point the admin UI/server proxy at the MAIN app origin only (https://... no trailing slash)
# BYANAI_API_BASE_URL=
# Same string as INTERNAL_API_SECRET on the main app, sent as X-Internal-API-Key
# INTERNAL_API_KEY=   (or whatever the admin project reads)
